@startuml seq_boot_security_fail
title SC-BOOT-02 - Security access failures in the PBL

participant "UDS tester" as Tester
box "TCU"
participant "PBL" as PBL
end box

note over Tester, PBL
Covers: SYS-BOOT-005, SYS-BOOT-009, SYS-DIA-001, SIM-TST-002
UDS requests on DIAG_PhysReq 0x7E1, responses on DIAG_Resp 0x7E9 (can_matrix section 5).
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

note over PBL: PBL programming session (boot window, or 10 02 from the default session),\nsecurity level 0x11 locked

== download without security access ==
Tester -> PBL : 34 00 44 04 00 00 00 <memSize>
PBL --> Tester : 7F 34 33
note right: securityAccessDenied (reprogramming section 3);\nthe PBL accepts the SBL download only after 27 (SYS-BOOT-005)

== wrong key ==
loop attempts 1 and 2
  Tester -> PBL : 27 11
  PBL --> Tester : 67 11 <seed, 4 bytes>
  Tester -> PBL : 27 12 <wrong key>
  PBL --> Tester : 7F 27 35
  note right: invalidKey (ISO 14229-1)
end
Tester -> PBL : 27 11
PBL --> Tester : 67 11 <seed, 4 bytes>
Tester -> PBL : 27 12 <wrong key> (attempt 3)
PBL --> Tester : 7F 27 36
note right: exceededNumberOfAttempts after 3 failed attempts (SYS-BOOT-005)
note over PBL: t0 = third failed attempt

== lockout for 10 s ==
Tester -> PBL : 27 11
PBL --> Tester : 7F 27 37
note right: requiredTimeDelayNotExpired: every 27 within 10 s after t0\n(SYS-BOOT-005, reprogramming section 3)
loop every 2 s during the delay
  Tester -> PBL : 3E 80 (0x7DF, no response)
  note right: keeps the session; without any request for 5000 ms\nthe PBL resets (SYS-BOOT-009, SC-BOOT-06)
end
... t0 + 10 s ...
Tester -> PBL : 27 11
PBL --> Tester : 67 11 <seed, 4 bytes>
Tester -> PBL : 27 12 <key = rotl32(seed, 7) XOR 0x5A3C_C3A5>
PBL --> Tester : 67 12
note right of PBL: level 0x11 unlocked; programming continues at step 7 (SC-BOOT-01)

note over Tester, PBL: The failed-attempt counter and the delay are not kept across a reset; a reset gives 3 new attempts (reprogramming section 3, accepted for v1).
@enduml
